+# Merge-chain Fleet PRE exact-SHA enforcement gate — 2026-09-16
+
+## Task
+Close GAP B: add a permanent, fail-closed merge-chain gate that machine-requires an exact-SHA Fleet PRE `READY_FOR_OCEAN` certificate before any PR head may be accepted for Ocean integration. Pure CI/scripts/tests/data/docs delta — no app/game/runtime change, no production deployment.
+
+## Why
+Weakest `CLAIM_TRUTH` control-plane pillar. Integration can proceed today with NO independent exact-SHA Fleet PRE certificate (proven: #116/#117/#121 merged without certs, plus the repeated #91/#113 false-green bypass class). Confirmed-error-twice => permanent regression-guard candidate; the Architect dispatch of 2026-09-16 (issue #80) defines acceptance A1-A6 for this exact delta.
+
+## Current state
+`master` = `414179ead82c97375f057e8e39a22c67dd981814` (`fix(autodemo): use live Creature Factory visuals (#121)`). GAP A (fail-closed Cloudflare) is already CLOSED on master via merged PR #117. GAP B remains OPEN: whole-tree grep for `FLEET_PRE`/`PRE_INTEGRATION_QA`/`READY_FOR_OCEAN` = zero enforcement occurrences. Worktree branch `opencode/merge-chain-fleet-pre-gate` created from `origin/master` `414179ea`; nothing else changed yet.
+
+## Target state
+A `fleet-pre-merge-chain` status check appears on PRs targeting master: no cert => red BLOCK; a fresh exact-SHA `READY_FOR_OCEAN` certificate (Fleet comment on issue #80) => green. The pure-Node checker and its 7 fail-closed rules + happy path are covered by `node --test` tests inside the required `check` gate.
+
+## Files / systems involved
+- `scripts/check-fleet-pre-certificate.cjs` (new, pure Node, no deps, `module.exports` for offline tests)
+- `.github/workflows/fleet-pre-merge-chain.yml` (new required PR check)
+- `test/fleet-pre-certificate.test.js` (new, 9 tests incl. bypass-class scan)
+- `data/fleet-pre-certificates/README.md` (new cert format/authority documentation)
+- `WORK_IN_PROGRESS.md` (this entry)
+
+## Known risks
+- The checked-in `data/fleet-pre-certificates/<sha>.json` file source must NOT be used as CI authority (a PR author can forge it in their own PR); CI uses the issue-#80 comment source only (Fleet comments require a repo collaborator). File source is deterministic validation only, documented fail-closed.
+- A single-header/decoding bug could make the gate trivially green — mitigated by 8 rule tests + a YAML bypass-class scan test (no `|| true`, no `continue-on-error`, no `if: always()` green).
+- The gate is designed to stay RED until a real Fleet PRE certifies the exact head; that is intended behavior, not a defect.
+
+## Golden systems that must be preserved
+The existing 5 protected required checks (check, quality-regression, agent-rules, world-quality, godot-web-preview), branch protection strictness on master, deny-by-default release, Vercel quota guard (`.github/` already non-deployable), exact-SHA freshness/provenance rules and Zero-Chaos.
